              "text": "Several established law firms in and immediately around **Mount Gravatt** and **Sunnybank** handle wills and estates with a focus on estate litigation, contesting wills, and Family Provision Applications (FPAs) under the *Succession Act 1981* (Qld).\n\n---\n\n### **Mount Gravatt & Upper Mount Gravatt**\n\n* **Bennett Carroll Solicitors (Upper Mount Gravatt)**  \n  * **Location:** Sanders Street, Upper Mount Gravatt  \n  * **Specialisation:** A prominent firm with a dedicated litigation and estate disputes practice. They frequently represent both claimants seeking provision and executors defending estates against Family Provision Applications. They also handle complex validity disputes (e.g., lack of testamentary capacity, fraud, and undue influence).\n* **Life Law Solutions (Mount Gravatt East)**  \n  * **Location:** Mount Gravatt East  \n  * **Specialisation:** Focuses heavily on relationship law, estate administration, and estate litigation. They regularly act in Supreme and District Court matters involving contested estates, inadequate provision claims, and mediation for disputed inheritances.\n* **Elliott & Harvey Lawyers (Upper Mount Gravatt)**  \n  * **Location:** Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt  \n  * **Specialisation:** A long-standing Southside boutique firm. Their succession team represents disappointed beneficiaries bringing FPAs, handles executor disputes, and manages negotiated settlements or court actions for disputed estates.\n* **Law Empire (Upper Mount Gravatt)**  \n  * **Location:** Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt  \n  * **Specialisation:** Focuses on succession and business law, offering representation for contested wills, executor breach claims, and family provision applications.\n\n---\n\n### **Sunnybank & Sunnybank Hills**\n\n* **Wheldon & Associates (Sunnybank)**  \n  * **Location:** Zamia Street, Sunnybank  \n  * **Specialisation:** A well-established Sunnybank practice that explicitly provides Supreme Court estate litigation services. They assist with challenging/defending the validity of wills, letters of administration disputes, and mediating family estate conflicts.\n* **CG Legal Group (Sunnybank Hills)**  \n  * **Location:** Sunnybank Hills  \n  * **Specialisation:** Practice covers commercial and estate law, with dedicated services for estate litigation, FPA dispute resolution, and contested wills.\n* **Madsen Law (Sunnybank)**  \n  * **Location:** Sunnybank  \n  * **Specialisation:** With a background spanning over two decades on Brisbane’s southside, they handle family and estate law, including advising clients excluded from wills or disputing the fairness of an estate distribution.\n\n---\n\n### **Notable Dedicated Specialist Just Nearby (Brisbane Southside)**\n\n* **Mitchells Solicitors / Estate Battles (Moorooka)**  \n  * **Location:** Beaudesert Road, Moorooka *(approx. 10 minutes from Mount Gravatt/Sunnybank)*  \n  * **Why consider them:** Led by Bryan Mitchell (a Queensland Law Society Accredited Specialist in Succession Law), Mitchells is one of Brisbane Southside’s most prominent niche firms for will disputes. They operate a dedicated arm (*Estate Battles*) devoted exclusively to estate litigation, lack of capacity claims, and Family Provision claims.\n\n---\n\n### **Important Considerations for Contesting a Will in Queensland**\n* **Strict Statutory Deadlines:** Under Queensland law, you must provide written notice of an intended Family Provision Application to the executor within **6 months** of the deceased’s date of death, and the formal court application must be filed within **9 months** of death. \n* **Funding:** Many estate litigation firms on the Southside offer an initial assessment to determine the merits of your claim, and some can act on a deferred-fee or \"no-win, no-fee\" basis for strong family provision cases.",
